00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:14.780
- They're all friends, because

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.220
- They're all related,
and they're all friends.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.560
There's no ghosting with The Royals.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.160
Because you're like, "Oh, I
hope I never see my ex again.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.240
Wait, it's also my cousin.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.120
Oh, and she's dating my brother now,

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.036
because there's no one else
we're allowed to date."

00:09:28.036 --> 00:09:28.957
- Would you marry a Royal?

00:09:28.957 --> 00:09:29.959
- Uh, no.

00:09:29.959 --> 00:09:31.630
Do you think a Royal would have me?

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:32.463
- Yes.

00:09:32.463 --> 00:09:33.330
- I'm very Milli Shand.
- Definitely.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.200
- What?
- [Kate] No.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.575
- With my trash mouth and slutty history?

00:09:36.575 --> 00:09:37.585
(jazz music)

00:09:37.585 --> 00:09:40.320
(typing sounds)

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:43.120
- Princess Margaret has an
affair, starts an affair,

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.521
with Roddy Llewellyn, who is this young,

00:09:45.521 --> 00:09:48.300
aristocratic, landscape gardener.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.730
- [Katherine] Why would an aristocrat

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.609
be a landscape gardener?

00:09:51.609 --> 00:09:53.270
- So, he's a creative sort of guy,

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:54.930
he wants to do something different.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:55.763
- Good for him.

00:09:55.763 --> 00:09:57.450
So, he's almost rebelling
against his rich family

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.634
by being like, "I'll show you,

00:09:58.634 --> 00:10:00.020
I'm gonna be a gardener."

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.470
- And he's young, he's finding his feet,

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:03.450
doing various things,

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.621
doing landscape gardening.
- I think he just wants to

00:10:04.621 --> 00:10:06.930
find himself off his feet,

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:07.970
if I can be honest,

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:11.980
because where do you find
rich and powerful older women?

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.470
By being a gardener.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.770
- She was very unhappy
in her marriage because

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:18.900
Lord Snowden, her husband,
had a lot of affairs.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:22.100
And Lord Snowden got a lot of support,

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:24.092
and Margaret really felt as if The Family,

00:10:24.092 --> 00:10:27.790
she said he was very oily
with the family, very oily.

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.861
So she felt excluded,
and when Roddy pops up,

00:10:30.861 --> 00:10:32.704
well, it's really-

00:10:32.704 --> 00:10:33.537
- He's a different oily.

00:10:33.537 --> 00:10:34.906
(Kate laughs)

00:10:34.906 --> 00:10:35.781
- Different oily.

00:10:35.781 --> 00:10:37.630
There's a lot of criticism of Margaret.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:40.470
The public opinion, and
also the politicians,

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.170
they called her a Royal Parasite.

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:44.070
They said, "We're all
tightening our belts,

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:46.030
and she's off with a toy boy."

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:48.560
And, you can imagine,
the prejudice there was

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.508
about an older woman and a younger man.

00:10:50.508 --> 00:10:51.500
- Yeah.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.360
And if I had known that
Margaret was that cool

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.750
before she died,

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.750
I probably would have made
a bigger deal of her death.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:11:00.300
Every February, I'm gonna
have Princess Margaret Day.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.133
- Okay.

00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:02.370
- And it's gonna be February 14th,

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:03.610
because that's Valentine's Day,

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.740
and that's just like a commercial holiday,

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.751
that we should better spend it,

00:11:07.751 --> 00:11:09.730
thinking about Princess Margaret.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.563
- [Kate] Can I come?

00:11:10.563 --> 00:11:11.396
- Yeah!

00:11:11.396 --> 00:11:12.229
- Great!

00:11:12.229 --> 00:11:13.210
- It's gonna be on a Caribbean Island,

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.130
and it will be immaculately landscaped.

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.341
We can have all our bushes trimmed,

00:11:17.341 --> 00:11:18.174
(Kate laughs)

00:11:18.174 --> 00:11:20.600
snog some Presidents, smoke it up.

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.913
I don't smoke, but I'll learn.

00:11:21.913 --> 00:11:22.746
(orchestra music)

00:11:22.746 --> 00:11:23.620
Thank you, Kate, for joining me

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.520
In my lavish library.
- Thank you.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:27.444
- You've answered so many
questions and enlightened me

00:11:27.444 --> 00:11:29.250
about the Royal Family.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.210
I hope you've been enlightened as well.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:33.200
They're pretty cool, especially Margaret.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.510
- But I think we should
definitely do our Margaret Day.

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:36.794
- February 14th!

00:11:36.794 --> 00:11:39.627
(orchestra music)

